{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-exp-finite-field-obstruction","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-exp-finite-field-obstruction","kind":"remark","title":"Finite-field obstruction for $\\exp_q$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-exponential","tags":["q-exponential","finite-field","characteristic-p","obstruction"],"text":"q-exp-finite-field-obstruction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-exp-finite-field-obstruction\"></a><p>The archimedean Taylor series <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q(x) = \\sum_{n \\ge 0} x^n / [n]_q!</code> fails over a field of characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> whenever the Jackson factorial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[n]_q!</code> vanishes modulo <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>. The grouplike <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q</code> nonetheless exists as a symbol in the formal Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{H}_q \\otimes \\mathbb{F}_p</code>. The truncated <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-exponential <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\exp_q^{(p)}(x) = \\sum_{n = 0}^{p - 1} x^n / [n]_q!</code> becomes grouplike modulo <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x^p = 0</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-exp-finite-field-obstruction.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.22.5"}
